%erg 0.1
Title: Cut the sitter's first tagged release and give it a working update path
Created: 2026-09-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-10T09:45Z claude created
2026-09-10T09:56Z claude note Filed alongside 0763 as the other half of the sitter release cut line. The gap that motivates it was found by reading update.json against `gh release list` and `git tag`, both of which are empty: the plugin as it stands can be installed and can never be updated.

--- body ---
## Context

The repository has **no tags and no GitHub releases** (`git tag` and
`gh release list -R MinhHaDuong/search-works-for-zotero` are both empty), and
`plugins/sdt-sitter/update.json` carries **no `update_link`**. Its own comment
says why, and the reasoning was correct at the time: the entry is "absent rather
than pointed at a release that does not exist".

The consequence is that a user who installs the sitter can never receive an
update. The host resolves `update_url`, finds one entry equal to the installed
version, and correctly concludes there is nothing newer — forever, because no
later entry can carry a link to fetch. Today that costs nothing, since the only
install path is a hand-delivered `.xpi` from the author. It is a release
blocker the moment anyone else installs it.

This is also the one change that moves the install path off the mechanism every
occurrence in ticket 0727 used. 0727 (the sitter disappearing from the installed
list, cause still open) is **not** a gate on this release — see the release-train
reasoning — but it is the reason the live check below is a fresh-profile install
*from the release asset* rather than from a local file.

DECISIONS.md ratified on 2026-09-06 that the sitter's permanent home is this
repo, as a workshop deliverable. Releasing it from here is consistent with that
ruling and with README.md's framing; it is not a change of shipping policy for
anything else in the tree.

## Relevant files

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/update.json` — the Mozilla update manifest, served raw from
  `main`; currently one entry, version 0.3.39, no `update_link`
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/manifest.json` — version 0.3.39, `update_url` at
  `raw.githubusercontent.com/.../main/plugins/sdt-sitter/update.json`,
  `strict_min_version` 10.0.1, `strict_max_version` 10.*
- `bench/check_sitter_version.py` — the `sitter-version` gate (Makefile:239);
  today it asserts no two payloads answer to one manifest version
- `bench/build_sdt_sitter.py` — builds the `.xpi`
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/RELEASE-NOTES.md:44` — "This draft does not claim a
  live-profile deployment or a published release"

## Actions

1. Settle the version. **0.4.0 proposed** — the 0.3.x series is the hand-delivered
   experimental line, and a first public tag deserves a boundary. Bump
   `manifest.json` and `update.json` in one commit; they may never disagree.
2. Build the `.xpi` and attach it to a signed tag (`/release` owns the signing
   step; it is human-only).
3. `update.json` gains `update_link` pointing at the release asset URL.
4. Extend `bench/check_sitter_version.py` to assert the three agree: manifest
   version == update.json version == the tag it claims, and `update_link` names
   an asset that exists. Today the gate reads the payload history only.
5. RELEASE-NOTES.md: drop the "does not claim ... a published release" sentence,
   and add a plain recovery line for 0727 — if the sitter disappears from
   Tools → Add-ons, restart Zotero, reinstall, and report it.

## Test

Red step first: point `update_link` at an asset that does not exist and confirm
the extended `check_sitter_version.py` fails. Then point it at the real one and
confirm it passes. A gate that cannot fail on a wrong link is not a gate, and
this one is guarding a URL nobody will read again.

## Verification

- [ ] Fresh Zotero profile, install from the **release asset URL**, restart,
      still present and active after thirty minutes of ordinary use. This is the
      released user's arm, and it is the arm 0727 has never had.
- [ ] An installed copy sees a bumped `update.json` and offers the update — or,
      if it does not, the log records what was observed rather than what was
      expected.
- [ ] `make check` passes, including the extended version gate.

## Invariants

- **Do not remove `update_url`.** 0727 established with a control that a build
  identical but for its removal is refused at install with "peut-être
  incompatible avec cette version de Zotero". This corrected 0688's docs-based
  reading; do not re-derive it the hard way.
- `strict_min_version` 10.0.1 and `strict_max_version` 10.* stay as declared in
  both files.
- The empty `updates` list is never restored: it is 0727's original suspected
  mechanism, and update.json's comment is the record of why.

## Exit criteria

A tag exists, a release carries the `.xpi`, `update.json` names it, and the
version gate asserts all three agree and has been shown red once by a deliberate
break. RELEASE-NOTES.md no longer disclaims a published release. 0727 stays open
as the recurrence trigger; this ticket does not close it and does not claim its
cause.
